1
00:00:11,344 --> 00:00:13,304
I gave you fair warning.

2
00:00:13,388 --> 00:00:16,725
Wow, a warning.
I never even got one in track.

3
00:00:17,267 --> 00:00:21,062
Wouldn't you be indignant
if you died doing something stupid?

4
00:00:27,861 --> 00:00:31,740
So what exactly is this passageway?

5
00:00:33,241 --> 00:00:35,118
Is it for managing the part-time jobs?

6
00:00:37,787 --> 00:00:38,913
That's a trade secret.

7
00:00:38,997 --> 00:00:40,331
Secret, my foot.

8
00:00:40,415 --> 00:00:42,625
Are you sure this leads us to Hyeok-jun?

9
00:00:43,668 --> 00:00:46,171
How much further do we have to go?

10
00:01:00,894 --> 00:01:02,437
Is this the right place?

11
00:01:58,827 --> 00:02:02,455
DEAD-END JOB

12
00:02:03,581 --> 00:02:06,543
LAST CARNIVAL

13
00:02:15,426 --> 00:02:19,472
Now, let's begin
<i>Challenge! A Father's Miracle!</i>

14
00:02:21,808 --> 00:02:28,273
A thrilling, heartwarming show
the whole family can enjoy together.

15
00:02:28,857 --> 00:02:31,818
The father has stayed up
five nights practicing.

16
00:02:31,901 --> 00:02:36,865
If he works a miracle in the studio today,
the family's wish will come true.

17
00:02:37,699 --> 00:02:40,535
- Now, <i>Challenge! A Father's Miracle.</i>
- This is insane.

18
00:02:40,618 --> 00:02:42,704
It's time to bring out our star.

19
00:02:42,787 --> 00:02:43,746
Mr. Byeon Min-su.

20
00:02:43,830 --> 00:02:45,498
- Come on out!
- Come on out!

21
00:03:02,432 --> 00:03:06,311
The father's mission today
is juggling while riding a unicycle.

22
00:03:06,811 --> 00:03:10,481
Will the father be able
to make his family's wish come true?

23
00:03:24,037 --> 00:03:25,455
Dad!

24
00:03:29,584 --> 00:03:30,710
Hyeok-jun.

25
00:03:31,419 --> 00:03:33,671
Dad, don't do that.

26
00:03:35,465 --> 00:03:36,591
Don't do it.

27
00:03:39,385 --> 00:03:40,887
What are you talking about?

28
00:03:42,013 --> 00:03:43,556
Why are you over there?

29
00:03:44,265 --> 00:03:45,558
You shouldn't be there.

30
00:03:46,476 --> 00:03:47,810
Hyeok-jun, come here.

31
00:03:48,436 --> 00:03:50,897
Come on, Hyeok-jun. Come over here.

32
00:03:54,192 --> 00:03:55,276
Hyeok-jun!

33
00:04:03,326 --> 00:04:04,244
Dad?

34
00:04:30,520 --> 00:04:31,646
Wait!

35
00:06:25,968 --> 00:06:31,307
I should just die.

36
00:06:32,308 --> 00:06:36,270
I should just die.

37
00:06:36,354 --> 00:06:37,230
Dad.

38
00:07:06,050 --> 00:07:07,218
No.

39
00:07:14,767 --> 00:07:17,478
"FANTASY" HAUNTED HOUSE

40
00:08:32,428 --> 00:08:34,847
Why are you hesitating
when you're so close?

41
00:08:39,477 --> 00:08:42,188
- Yeon-Joo.
- Aren't you going to open the door?

42
00:08:45,066 --> 00:08:45,900
Why?

43
00:08:47,151 --> 00:08:51,322
Are you afraid that if you do,
monsters will appear and not your father?

44
00:08:56,494 --> 00:08:57,537
Or

45
00:08:58,955 --> 00:09:00,998
you'll find out
your father is now a monster?

46
00:09:05,670 --> 00:09:08,422
Just what exactly is behind this door?

47
00:09:09,006 --> 00:09:10,466
The other world.

48
00:09:12,426 --> 00:09:14,136
But I can't really remember it.

49
00:09:17,014 --> 00:09:19,183
I've been trapped in darkness so long,

50
00:09:20,643 --> 00:09:23,062
and all I've wanted was to go back.

51
00:09:25,398 --> 00:09:26,732
Don't you think…

52
00:09:30,945 --> 00:09:32,405
it'd be the same for your father?

53
00:09:57,263 --> 00:09:58,973
Things must've gone awry.

54
00:10:00,224 --> 00:10:01,100
Move.

55
00:10:10,234 --> 00:10:12,737
You guys ruined everything!

56
00:11:00,743 --> 00:11:04,080
You're not really much help,

57
00:11:04,580 --> 00:11:06,374
so why don't you just wait here?

58
00:11:06,874 --> 00:11:09,627
You wait here!
I have to go find him, damn it!

59
00:11:16,509 --> 00:11:17,677
Yeon-joo!

60
00:11:52,878 --> 00:11:54,547
Don't just take it lying down.

61
00:11:55,631 --> 00:11:57,633
At least put up a fight
if you want to live.

62
00:12:00,428 --> 00:12:03,389
You almost died several times
trying to make money.

63
00:12:05,099 --> 00:12:06,559
Do you still not get

64
00:12:08,060 --> 00:12:09,729
what kind of world this is?

65
00:12:15,526 --> 00:12:16,736
Back away!

66
00:12:18,446 --> 00:12:19,905
I'll buy some time.

67
00:12:19,989 --> 00:12:23,075
We can change the world
only if you open this door now.

68
00:12:24,243 --> 00:12:25,786
So you must open it.

69
00:12:25,870 --> 00:12:27,663
Where's this coming from all of a sudden?

70
00:12:29,373 --> 00:12:30,416
Yeon-joo!

71
00:12:34,837 --> 00:12:36,672
If you open that door,

72
00:12:37,798 --> 00:12:40,926
all beings from that world
will surge into this one.

73
00:12:41,677 --> 00:12:43,429
The world will be destroyed!

74
00:12:44,263 --> 00:12:45,890
Don't listen to him.

75
00:12:47,016 --> 00:12:49,727
That side's no different,
since everything came from this one.

76
00:12:53,272 --> 00:12:54,231
Move aside.

77
00:12:56,525 --> 00:12:57,902
That woman is a monster.

78
00:12:59,153 --> 00:12:59,987
Move!

79
00:13:14,960 --> 00:13:16,754
Go back to where you came from.

80
00:13:33,938 --> 00:13:35,356
We meet at last.

81
00:13:44,365 --> 00:13:46,033
What? That didn't do anything?

82
00:13:49,912 --> 00:13:51,205
Let go.

83
00:13:54,041 --> 00:13:55,292
I said, "Let go!"

84
00:14:02,758 --> 00:14:03,759
Stop it!

85
00:14:06,679 --> 00:14:08,138
Mr. Byeon Hyeok-jun!

86
00:14:08,222 --> 00:14:10,558
You're here to work, so just work!

87
00:14:10,641 --> 00:14:12,768
Get a grip, will you?

88
00:14:14,812 --> 00:14:16,146
You need to make money!

89
00:14:19,567 --> 00:14:21,068
You need money.

90
00:14:25,197 --> 00:14:26,073
Hey.

91
00:14:27,366 --> 00:14:31,662
Do you know how many people have died
at these part-time jobs?

92
00:14:38,377 --> 00:14:40,337
Do you know how many I've saved?

93
00:14:41,881 --> 00:14:44,091
You wanted to kill yourselves anyway!

94
00:14:44,633 --> 00:14:47,553
I made your hopeless lives useful!

95
00:15:02,860 --> 00:15:06,780
We must offer sacrifices
to save more people.

96
00:15:09,199 --> 00:15:11,619
That's how the world works.

97
00:15:13,495 --> 00:15:15,998
Good-for-nothing people like you

98
00:15:16,498 --> 00:15:18,584
should at least help out like this.

99
00:15:19,376 --> 00:15:20,336
Don't you agree?

100
00:15:23,005 --> 00:15:25,591
I even raised your wages a lot, didn't I?

101
00:15:29,136 --> 00:15:31,513
Nothing's free in this world.

102
00:15:35,059 --> 00:15:37,102
They were all trying to live.

103
00:15:39,563 --> 00:15:40,606
What did you say?

104
00:15:45,402 --> 00:15:47,738
They didn't do the jobs
to throw their lives away.

105
00:15:49,198 --> 00:15:51,200
They did it to live.

106
00:15:59,249 --> 00:16:01,627
You sound just like your dad.

107
00:16:08,634 --> 00:16:09,468
No.

108
00:16:23,357 --> 00:16:25,067
No!

109
00:16:51,218 --> 00:16:53,804
How does it feel to be alive?

110
00:17:01,812 --> 00:17:03,772
Now you be the one who dies.

111
00:17:26,962 --> 00:17:27,796
How…

112
00:17:30,299 --> 00:17:31,508
How are you…

113
00:17:32,051 --> 00:17:33,302
Thanks to you, Hyeok-jun…

114
00:17:35,721 --> 00:17:41,393
now people will know
what the world is really like.

115
00:17:48,484 --> 00:17:49,818
Thanks to me?

116
00:17:50,694 --> 00:17:54,156
- How can so many casualties change the--
- It's been 40 years.

117
00:17:56,742 --> 00:18:00,621
But this world hasn't changed.
It's become even more rotten and complex.

118
00:18:04,249 --> 00:18:06,627
This was the only way to set things right.

119
00:18:09,880 --> 00:18:11,965
Instead of one person dying unjustly…

120
00:18:14,051 --> 00:18:15,135
everyone will equally…

121
00:18:17,346 --> 00:18:18,639
perish together.

122
00:18:21,642 --> 00:18:22,976
I'm sorry I deceived you.

123
00:19:18,073 --> 00:19:19,074
Dad.

124
00:19:30,377 --> 00:19:32,087
Come on. Let's go home.

125
00:19:32,171 --> 00:19:34,047
I don't care about money,

126
00:19:34,840 --> 00:19:36,466
so don't ever do jobs like this again.

127
00:19:37,050 --> 00:19:37,885
Let's go.

128
00:19:40,179 --> 00:19:41,263
No.

129
00:19:45,475 --> 00:19:47,311
I can't go.

130
00:20:09,082 --> 00:20:10,125
Excuse me.

131
00:20:13,212 --> 00:20:15,672
If you meet my family on the other side,

132
00:20:17,049 --> 00:20:19,092
could you please give this to them?

133
00:20:33,482 --> 00:20:36,735
It's not much, but I'd appreciate it.

134
00:20:42,824 --> 00:20:43,992
Also,

135
00:20:45,535 --> 00:20:47,412
you shouldn't be here.

136
00:20:49,331 --> 00:20:50,791
You'll end up like me.

137
00:21:00,259 --> 00:21:01,718
Get out of here now.

138
00:21:02,469 --> 00:21:04,388
The door shouldn't be open.

139
00:21:04,972 --> 00:21:05,973
<i>Oppa!</i>

140
00:21:06,056 --> 00:21:07,683
Byeon Hyeok-jun!

141
00:21:07,766 --> 00:21:09,393
Snap out of it!

142
00:21:10,227 --> 00:21:12,729
Byeon Hyeok-jun, please!
Get a hold of yourself!

143
00:21:22,990 --> 00:21:23,949
Byeon Hyeok-jun!

144
00:21:27,661 --> 00:21:28,704
Please!

145
00:21:58,608 --> 00:21:59,443
Hey.

146
00:22:07,326 --> 00:22:08,618
Come on!

147
00:22:36,772 --> 00:22:37,939
Is it over?

148
00:22:50,035 --> 00:22:51,036
<i>Attention, please.</i>

149
00:22:51,119 --> 00:22:52,913
- Let's go!
- <i>A fire has been reported.</i>

150
00:22:52,996 --> 00:22:57,542
<i>Please evacuate immediately</i>
<i>to a safe area using the exits.</i>

151
00:22:57,626 --> 00:22:59,336
<i>Attention, please.</i>
<i>A fire has been reported.</i>

152
00:23:00,003 --> 00:23:02,214
- Wait. Open it.
- Hey!

153
00:23:02,297 --> 00:23:03,590
Hurry!

154
00:23:04,216 --> 00:23:05,217
Come on!

155
00:23:12,391 --> 00:23:13,642
Oh, goodness.

156
00:23:21,525 --> 00:23:23,026
Let's go home now.

157
00:23:26,405 --> 00:23:29,616
<i>See you again, again</i>

158
00:23:30,492 --> 00:23:33,620
<i>Moments we've dreamt of</i>

159
00:23:33,703 --> 00:23:36,998
<i>Our own Neo World</i>

160
00:23:50,595 --> 00:23:51,930
<i>The world did not end.</i>

161
00:23:55,350 --> 00:23:56,810
<i>It did not end…</i>

162
00:23:58,937 --> 00:24:00,397
<i>nor did it change.</i>

163
00:24:03,191 --> 00:24:05,235
See? We should've hired another worker.

164
00:24:06,820 --> 00:24:07,737
I'm sorry.

165
00:24:10,824 --> 00:24:11,867
I'm exhausted.

166
00:24:11,950 --> 00:24:16,455
But still, you do excellent work.

167
00:24:16,538 --> 00:24:18,039
Did you work part-time much?

168
00:24:20,667 --> 00:24:21,501
Yeah, well,

169
00:24:22,169 --> 00:24:23,044
I've worked a lot.

170
00:24:23,128 --> 00:24:25,172
<i>We are back living together</i>
<i>in a small house</i>…

171
00:24:25,255 --> 00:24:27,507
- Why'd you bring the fridge?
- You gave it to me.

172
00:24:27,591 --> 00:24:28,884
<i>…but it isn't all bad.</i>

173
00:24:28,967 --> 00:24:31,344
- What are you doing?
- Fine, I won't pour it.

174
00:24:31,428 --> 00:24:33,221
<i>- We eat together.</i>
- It's always dip.

175
00:24:34,055 --> 00:24:34,890
What happened?

176
00:24:34,973 --> 00:24:37,350
<i>And when we do,</i>
<i>it feels like nothing ever happened.</i>

177
00:24:37,434 --> 00:24:38,894
I put it outside.

178
00:24:41,813 --> 00:24:42,814
<i>Although…</i>

179
00:24:50,780 --> 00:24:52,032
<i>it wasn't all a dream.</i>

180
00:25:09,508 --> 00:25:10,592
<i>But now,</i>

181
00:25:11,968 --> 00:25:13,428
<i>it's all in the past.</i>

182
00:25:19,226 --> 00:25:20,769
Smile, please.

183
00:25:21,853 --> 00:25:22,687
"I'm confident."

184
00:25:24,189 --> 00:25:26,191
That's it!

185
00:25:26,691 --> 00:25:30,403
Goodness, with your good looks,
you'll get hired anywhere.

186
00:25:32,489 --> 00:25:33,490
Yes, you will.

187
00:26:04,479 --> 00:26:05,313
Excuse me!

188
00:26:13,572 --> 00:26:14,531
Damn it!

189
00:26:19,119 --> 00:26:19,995
Excuse me.

190
00:26:23,456 --> 00:26:24,624
Are you okay?

191
00:26:26,668 --> 00:26:29,170
Why did you have to save me?

192
00:26:30,714 --> 00:26:31,756
What?

193
00:26:31,840 --> 00:26:32,841
Do you have any idea

194
00:26:33,883 --> 00:26:34,843
how much it took

195
00:26:35,760 --> 00:26:38,471
for me to come here?

196
00:26:41,182 --> 00:26:44,269
I don't have it in me to go on,
and I'm broke.

197
00:26:45,562 --> 00:26:47,314
No, but still, this is a bit--

198
00:26:47,397 --> 00:26:49,316
But still, what?

199
00:26:51,067 --> 00:26:54,070
I was in a similar situation
a long time ago.

200
00:26:54,154 --> 00:26:56,698
Not that I'm saying you're like me.

201
00:26:56,781 --> 00:27:00,452
So what I'm trying to say is…

202
00:27:26,645 --> 00:27:27,937
Thank you.

203
00:27:47,540 --> 00:27:51,127
DO YOU THINK IT'S ALL OVER?

204
00:27:54,422 --> 00:27:55,256
<i>Hyeok-jun.</i>

205
00:27:56,716 --> 00:27:58,885
- The food's here.
- Here's one <i>tteokbokki.</i>

206
00:27:58,968 --> 00:28:00,553
- Thank you.
- One <i>sundae.</i>

207
00:28:00,637 --> 00:28:02,055
- And one fritters.
- Thank you.

208
00:28:02,138 --> 00:28:04,683
- <i>Mysterious fires occurring nationwide…</i>
- Sure, enjoy.

209
00:28:04,766 --> 00:28:06,142
It looks good.

210
00:28:06,226 --> 00:28:07,477
- <i>Jeon reporting.</i>
- Eat up.

211
00:28:07,560 --> 00:28:09,562
<i>The police are actively investigating,</i>

212
00:28:09,646 --> 00:28:12,232
<i>but the cause of the serial fires</i>
<i>is still unknown.</i>

213
00:28:12,315 --> 00:28:14,859
<i>The National Forensic Service reports</i>

214
00:28:14,943 --> 00:28:20,532
<i>an unknown substance and unidentified DNA</i>
<i>were found at all the fire scenes.</i>

215
00:28:20,615 --> 00:28:24,285
<i>This is similar</i>
<i>to the explosion at Kyungil Neo World.</i>

216
00:28:24,369 --> 00:28:28,039
<i>With the recurrence of these unprecedented</i>
<i>and bizarre incidents, investigators…</i>

217
00:28:54,274 --> 00:28:55,900
Damn it.

218
00:29:10,707 --> 00:29:12,625
"Spider Staffing Agency manager"?

219
00:29:14,210 --> 00:29:15,879
"Predecessor's endorsement"?

220
00:29:25,138 --> 00:29:26,181
<i>Mr. Hyeok-jun.</i>

221
00:29:28,975 --> 00:29:31,936
<i>If you're listening to this message,</i>
<i>it's a shame.</i>

222
00:29:32,479 --> 00:29:34,606
<i>So the balance was broken in the end.</i>

223
00:29:36,107 --> 00:29:38,151
<i>You may not be entirely at fault,</i>

224
00:29:38,943 --> 00:29:42,989
<i>but if you accept this position,</i>
<i>you'll see a different truth.</i>

225
00:29:44,657 --> 00:29:48,620
<i>I'm curious if you'll come</i>
<i>to a different conclusion than I did.</i>

226
00:29:50,121 --> 00:29:51,164
<i>So how about it?</i>

227
00:29:51,247 --> 00:29:53,875
<i>Can you look the other way</i>
<i>and go on living?</i>

228
00:29:54,667 --> 00:29:55,543
<i>Or</i>

229
00:29:56,336 --> 00:29:57,754
<i>will you accept?</i>

230
00:30:47,345 --> 00:30:48,471
"Recruitment results…"

231
00:30:48,972 --> 00:30:51,599
"Congratulations on your success."

232
00:30:56,312 --> 00:30:57,564
"Kyungil Group"?

233
00:34:50,630 --> 00:34:53,132
ALL NAMES, EVENTS, BRANDS,
PERSONS, AND PLACES

234
00:34:53,216 --> 00:34:55,259
DEPICTED IN THIS SERIES ARE FICTIONAL

235
00:34:55,343 --> 00:34:57,637
ANY RESEMBLANCE TO REALITY IS COINCIDENTAL

236
00:34:58,638 --> 00:35:02,517
Subtitle translation by: Yung Un Choi
